<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter Jackson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1961</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sir Peter Jackson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter Jackson is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> film director and producer best known for The Lord of the Rings trilogy (2001–2003), filmed in New Zealand, whose final part won eleven Academy Awards. He also directed Heavenly Creatures, King Kong and The Hobbit trilogy. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wellington">Wellington</a> studios and effects companies helped build a film industry that made New Zealand's landscapes known worldwide.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-jackson.jpg" alt="Peter Jackson" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gage Skidmore · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_Jackson_SDCC_2014.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
